# PATENT CLAIMS

**Claim 1.** A roller-based label aligning device for precisely applying labels onto products, comprising:

a frame assembly defining a product transport path;

a label dispensing mechanism operatively coupled to the frame assembly, the label dispensing mechanism configured to feed a continuous web of label material toward the product transport path;

a peel plate positioned adjacent to the label dispensing mechanism, the peel plate configured to separate individual labels from the continuous web at a peel edge;

at least one alignment roller rotatably mounted to the frame assembly, the alignment roller having a resilient outer surface and being positioned to contact a separated label and apply the label onto a surface of a product traveling along the product transport path;

a sensor assembly configured to detect a position of the product relative to the product transport path and generate a position signal;

a control system operatively coupled to the sensor assembly and the alignment roller, the control system configured to adjust at least one of a rotational speed, a rotational timing, or a lateral position of the alignment roller based on the position signal to align the label with a predetermined target location on the product; and

a biasing mechanism coupled to the alignment roller, the biasing mechanism configured to apply a controlled contact pressure between the alignment roller and the product sufficient to adhere the label without displacing the product from the product transport path.

**Claim 2.** The device of claim 1, wherein the alignment roller comprises a plurality of rollers arranged in a sequential configuration along the product transport path, each roller configured to progressively apply and smooth the label onto the product surface.

**Claim 3.** The device of claim 1, wherein the resilient outer surface of the alignment roller comprises an elastomeric material having a durometer selected to conform to a contour of the product surface while maintaining sufficient rigidity to prevent label wrinkling.

**Claim 4.** The device of claim 1, further comprising a lateral positioning mechanism coupled to the alignment roller, the lateral positioning mechanism configured to translate the alignment roller in a direction transverse to the product transport path in response to the control system, thereby correcting a lateral misalignment of the label relative to the product.

**Claim 5.** The device of claim 1, wherein the sensor assembly comprises at least one of an optical sensor, a proximity sensor, a machine vision camera, or an encoder configured to determine a longitudinal position, a rotational orientation, or a lateral position of the product.

**Claim 6.** The device of claim 1, wherein the control system further comprises a feedback loop configured to compare the position signal to a stored reference position and generate a correction signal for adjusting the alignment roller in real time.

**Claim 7.** The device of claim 1, further comprising a tension control mechanism configured to regulate a tension of the continuous web of label material to maintain a consistent peel rate at the peel plate.

**Claim 8.** The device of claim 1, wherein the alignment roller includes an internal heating element configured to activate a heat-sensitive adhesive on the label prior to or during application onto the product surface.

**Claim 9.** The device of claim 1, wherein the control system is further configured to synchronize the rotational speed of the alignment roller with a linear speed of the product transport path to minimize label stretching or wrinkling during application.

**Claim 10.** The device of claim 1, further comprising a vacuum assist mechanism positioned proximate to the peel plate, the vacuum assist mechanism configured to hold the separated label in a fixed orientation prior to contact with the alignment roller.

**Claim 11.** A method for precisely applying labels onto products using a roller-based label aligning device, the method comprising:

feeding a continuous web of label material toward a peel plate;

separating an individual label from the continuous web at the peel plate;

detecting, via a sensor assembly, a position of a product traveling along a product transport path;

generating a position signal based on the detected position;

adjusting, via a control system, at least one of a rotational speed, a rotational timing, or a lateral position of an alignment roller based on the position signal;

contacting the separated label with the alignment roller; and

applying, via the alignment roller, the label onto a predetermined target location on a surface of the product under a controlled contact pressure sufficient to adhere the label without displacing the product.

**Claim 12.** The method of claim 11, further comprising progressively smoothing the label onto the product surface using a plurality of sequentially arranged alignment rollers.

**Claim 13.** The method of claim 11, further comprising translating the alignment roller in a direction transverse to the product transport path to correct a detected lateral misalignment of the label relative to the product.

**Claim 14.** The method of claim 11, further comprising synchronizing the rotational speed of the alignment roller with a linear speed of the product transport path.

**Claim 15.** The method of claim 11, further comprising regulating a tension of the continuous web of label material to maintain a consistent peel rate at the peel plate.

